      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1292435747,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Is this the name of the field in the spec? The name doesn't lend itself to the value being a boolean. For example, reading the positive or negative display filter, it's hard to know what they mean:\n\n* smpp.command_type\n* !smpp.command_type\n\nIf you want to use a boolean, then a field name like \"smpp.is_command\" sounds better. Or, if you want the name \"smpp.command_type\", then a an FT_UINT8 with a value_string works better.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8752203,
            "username": "gilramir",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gilbert Ramirez",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4b50ee5959de649feeeb66ab36b6de3d2b6f37a37df87082250b2e06516f2f1a?s=80&d=identicon",
